Phase 0 Master Audit & Map (Task #968) — re-work after code review

Adds a complete read-only audit of `easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/` under
`docs/audit/phase-0/` (11 markdown deliverables) and reproducible
inventory scripts under `scripts/audit/phase-0/` (8 bash + 2 Node
helpers). Zero application code changed.

What changed in this re-work:
- Inventory scripts rewritten to address review feedback:
  - `inventory-edge-functions.sh`: now builds an inter-function call
    graph (`fetch` + `functions.invoke` edges, 49 found) and emits
    shared-imports per function.
  - `inventory-tables-policies.sh`: per-column extraction with
    `file:line` provenance via `extract-columns.mjs` (9 271 column rows
    captured); RPC names now extracted explicitly.
  - `inventory-routes.sh`: page-file ↔ importer reachability diff
    (43 truly unreferenced page files identified).
  - New `inventory-rpc-orphans.sh`: builds an RPC orphan matrix and
    cross-checks against multi-line `CREATE TRIGGER … EXECUTE FUNCTION`
    targets via `extract-trigger-targets.mjs` (147 true orphan RPCs).
  - New `inventory-button-handlers.sh`: 76 single-line `<Button>` with
    no handler + 149 multi-line candidates.
- Reports rewritten with concrete `migration_file:line` provenance and
  `file:line` writer evidence; placeholder language ("queued",
  "manual review later", "will produce") replaced with confidence
  labels and named-symbol lists:
  - 03-dead-code-and-orphans.md
  - 04-conflicts-duplications.md
  - 05-flows-without-state-machine.md
  - 06-domain-ownership-map.md
- 00-readme.md updated: corrected RPC count (288 → 283) and added the
  two new scripts + Node helpers to the reproduction recipe.

Evidence (40 files in `99-evidence/`) regenerated end-to-end. All CSVs
have well-formed headers and consistent column counts.

Follow-up project tasks #977 (polling → realtime) and #978 (confirm
unused edge functions) were submitted previously and are not
re-submitted.
